pocket-motion-only: PATH is drawn by this software rasteriser alone, and every upstream backend parses the draw list by a closed op set — the PSP GE, the ESP32 and Symbian RGB565 hosts, Vita, gpui and wgpu would stop the frame at op 71; a path's coverage is a winding sum over any number of concave contours with 1/256 px vertices, which none of those targets has a primitive for.

0042 — vector paths, the op: a PATH TABLE in styles.bin, the geometry in
the core, and DRAW_OP.path (71). The design is
`patches/0042-vector-paths.design.md` in this repository, and its last
section records where the landing departs from the stage-1 prototype
(`baselines/vector-paths/prototype.diff`, on e0b37e2 + 0001-0022); the
numbers are `baselines/vector-paths.md`. `0043` is the declaration that
fills the table.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts` and the generated `spec.rs`, microts `spec.rs`
  and `component-types-microts.ts`: props `path` (199, int: table index + 1),
  `fillColor` 200, `fillRule` 201, `strokeColor` 202, `strokeWidth` 203,
  `strokeJoin` 204, `strokeCap` 205, `strokeMiter` 206, `trimStart` 207,
  `trimEnd` 208, `trimOffset` 209, `trimMode` 210, `morph` 211 — one block
  after `shutterHold` (198), because 187-197 are eleven ids and these are
  thirteen; anim bits 58-64 for the seven animatable ones (main's `skewX`
  moved the paint bits by one, so not stage 1's 57-63); enums `FillRule`,
  `StrokeJoin`, `StrokeCap`, `TrimMode`, and `BgClip.Path` (2);
  `DRAW_OP.path = 71` and its format comment; the PATH TABLE format, written
  after the ANIM TABLE and counted by the header's u16 at offset 10, which
  was reserved — so a table with no path is the bytes it was — with
  `encodeStyleTable`/`decodeStyleTable` writing and reading it and the
  encoder refusing what the core would.
- `engine/core/src/path.rs` (new): the entry and its parser (a first verb
  that is not a move, an unknown verb, 0 or more than 8 shapes, shapes of
  different point counts and a non-finite coordinate are refused); morph as
  `a * (1 - t) + b * t`, exact at every key; cubics flattened in local space
  by Wang's bound with the tolerance over the transform's Frobenius norm, so
  a turning path keeps its chord count; trim by arc length (each/whole, a
  wrapping offset, the whole window short-circuited byte for byte); the
  stroke as positively wound cycles whose nonzero fill is the union of its
  quads, join wedges and caps, round joins and caps by bisection with no
  trigonometry; and emission through the world affine (a viewBox composed
  in front, xMidYMid meet), clipped to the viewport grown by 4 px and
  quantised to 1/256 px. `fmath::sqrtf` behind a guard that reads a NaN as
  0; no other math function.
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: the op — a winding sum per sample on POLY's
  4x4 lattice with a top-left rule (an edge counts at sample row Y when
  ytop <= Y < ybot, a crossing at x for the samples with X >= x), in i64
  integers; edges bucketed by first row and stepped exactly by quotient and
  remainder; runs emitted, so an interior is one `fill_opaque`. `Clip`
  is crate-visible for the tests.
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: `emit_node_path` — after a node's ground and
  before its children, the fill (or under `bg-clip-path` its ground, a 0019
  gradient as PAINT_PUSH around a white fill), then the stroke; both carry
  the subtree opacity. `bg-clip-path` leaves the box unpainted.
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: the table parsed after the ANIM TABLE; the
  thirteen fields on `Resolved`.
- `engine/core/src/damage.rs`, `compositor.rs`, `lib.rs`: the three other
  walkers take PATH's length from its word 1 and refuse one shorter than its
  header, which would never advance; damage bounds a PATH by its vertices.
- `engine/core/src/path_scenes.rs` and `path_tests.rs` (new; the scenes are
  also behind the `path-scenes` feature, for the wasm harness in
  `baselines/vector-paths/pathwasm`), and `tests.rs`'s `validate_drawlist`,
  which holds every PATH vertex inside the guard band.

