(`baselines/vector-paths/runs/redcheck-0042.txt`). The five after `table:
shape count not bounded` were added at the landing.

Measured at the landing, on 66caf4e5 + 0001-0043 (darwin/arm64, rustc 1.97.1):
`cargo test --release` in `engine/core`, 291 tests pass, the 25 path
tests among them (stage 1's 24 and `every_draw_list_walker_steps_over_a_path`);
the printed measurements are stage 1's to the digit
(`baselines/vector-paths/runs/core-test-prints-0042.txt`). Fifteen of the sixteen pinned scenes reproduce stage 1's thirty
digests; scene 10 is re-pinned. Its MASK_PUSH was written in the format 0024
replaced, so the stream stopped at the mask and `path_under_a_mask_…`
compared two grounds — passing with nothing under test; both now go through
`mask_push`, and the test asserts the mask let paint through. With the mask
written correctly and 0032's exact divisor reverted, scene 10's framebuffer is
stage 1's 0xbb5836a02e7cc858 byte for byte, so the move is 0032's.
With 0042 and 0043 applied (`bun scripts/vendor.ts`: 66caf4e5 + 36
patches), the digest ledger reproduces all 38 compositions it recorded
before, unchanged — a styles.bin with no path is the bytes it was — and
records `compositions/vector-paths`, 39 of 39; the visibility ledger 46 of
46.

